{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b6ac54f1fb731071","name":"Escape from Kessel","source":{"id":"source:reference-b6ac54f1fb731071","title":"Escape from Kessel","revision":21172,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:17:48Z","sha256":"a014f6869d4256bd7278e535f4129ff7dea0a442381dce7273bab5974621d516","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21172","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Escape%20from%20Kessel&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b6ac54f1fb731071","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},", the heroes are trapped in the spice mines of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kessel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kessel","referenceId":"reference:c81eccaf20934088"}," and must escape to freedom. The spice mines are currently under the control of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoids?action=edit&redlink=1"},", an insectoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," responsible for the design of the Droideka. The heroes have a chance to escape while being herded back to their barracks, and their goal is to make their way out of the mines, through the detention facility, and out to a landing pad where a spice-hauling vessel is refueling for take-off. During the breakout, 10 other prisoners also decide to fight their way to freedom, helping the heroes escape.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Escape from Kessel Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Complexity:"]}," 2 (8 Successes before 3 Failures)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested Primary Skills for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," (DC 18):"]}," The heroes can keep their eyes and ears open for the signs of approaching ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoid?action=edit&redlink=1"}," guards. Alternatively, the heroes can search for side tunnels and passages that are rarely used."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," (DC 23):"]}," The heroes can convince some of their fellow prisoners to keep watch or fan out to distract the guards and prevent them from catching the main group."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," (DC 18):"]}," The heroes can attempt to sneak by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoid?action=edit&redlink=1"}," patrols and to ensure that none of the other prisoners makes too much noise."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Survival"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Survival","referenceId":"reference:8302496de0ace160"}," (DC 28):"]}," The heroes can search for signs of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoid?action=edit&redlink=1"}," tracks in the tunnels they are following, using that knowledge to determine which passages the insectoids are least likely to search."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Challenge Effects"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Challenge Effects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Challenge_Effects"}," for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Close Call"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Close_Call","referenceId":"reference:06e10d30642aaca6"},":"]}," The heroes accrue Failures only on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"}," that fail by 5 or more."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Degrees of Failure"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Degrees_of_Failure","referenceId":"reference:8d28a4bee6e70b14"},":"]}," Any Failures accrued by the heroes reduce the number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," prisoners that reach the ship and escape."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Success and Failure"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Success:"]}," If the heroes succeed, they make their way to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["GX1 Short Hauler"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/GX1_Short_Hauler?action=edit&redlink=1"}," sitting on the landing pad. They successfully steal the ship and jump into hyperspace.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Failure:"]}," If the heroes fail the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},", they are cornered by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoid?action=edit&redlink=1"}," guards and must engage in a difficult combat encounter to finally gain their freedom. If the heroes succeed but accrued one Failure during the challenge, only five of the other prisoners make it to freedom with them. If the heroes succeed but accrued two Failures during the challenge, none of the other prisoners reach the ",{"tag":"a","children":["GX1 Short Hauler"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/GX1_Short_Hauler?action=edit&redlink=1"},"- all 10 are recaptured by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colicoids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colicoids?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
